'''Sharkman Karate''' is a [[Fighting Styles|fighting style]] obtainable in the [[Second Sea]] and the [[Third Sea]].

Sharkman Karate has relatively low damage, especially compared with the v2 fighting styles. However, it makes up for this by offering excellent combo potential and stuns. However, it is a bit stronger than [[Water Kung Fu]] for grinding purposes. It also is great for breaking and starting combos, and offers a versatile moveset. 

Sharkman Karate can also be upgraded from the [[Sharkman Master]] [[NPCs|NPC]] in the [[Submerged Island]].

==Obtainment==
Sharkman Karate can be obtained from the [[Sharkman Teacher]] after giving him a [[Water Key]] and having [[Water Kung Fu]] at 400 mastery or more. The player needs to pay {{Money|2,500,000}} and {{Fragment|5,000}}.

The "{{Title|Sharkman}}" [[Titles|title]] #0130 will be granted upon obtaining this fighting style.

==Mastery==
* 400+ Mastery: Sharkman Karate is one of the requirements to obtain [[Godhuman]] in the [[Third Sea]].
* 500+ Mastery: Upgrades for the style become available at the [[Sharkman Master]].

==Upgrading==
Sharkman Karate's moveset can be upgraded by interacting, training and buying upgrades from the [[Sharkman Master]], with the interaction having a requirement of at least 500 mastery on the style and the player has to be level 2200
* Upgrading {{Ability|Z}} requires the [[Headband (Yellow)]] and {{fragment|2,000}}. Once upgraded, it allows the user to shoot out a shark after the palm rush.
* Upgrading {{Ability|X}} requires the [[Headband (Blue)]] and {{fragment|3,000}}. Once upgraded, it allows the user to control the positioning of the bubble encasing the enemy with their cursor or finger whilst holding the move.
* Upgrading {{Ability|C}} requires the [[Headband (Black)]] and {{fragment|5,000}}. Once upgraded, if hit, it grants the user a temporary shield that gives a 35% defense buff for a short while, similar to [[Shark]]'s [[Water Body|V3 ability]].
In total, upgrading all the moves costs {{fragment|10,000}}.

