==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Can work with many builds.
* Insane combo potential, even higher than [[Godhuman]] with the correct build.
* Precise knockback.
* Moves can [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].

|'''[Z] Twelve Water Palms'''
* Short cooldown.
* Good mobility.
* Fast casting.
* [[Instinct/Break|Breaks Instinct]].

|'''[X] Pressure Vortex'''
* Good range.
* [[Instinct/Break|Breaks Instinct]] on the 2nd hit.
* Strong [[stun]].
** Stronger stun when upgraded
** The strongest stun for any fighting style, only when upgraded and held fully.
* Controllable to a good degree (only when upgraded and held).
* The held version merges both of the hits into one, resulting in a guaranteed instinct break.
* Grabs upon contact with the shark (both versions, the tap version even if instinct-tricked)
* Very long range.
* Distorts the enemies screen (bubble).
* No knockback.

|'''[C] Great Sea Spear'''
* Can grab multiple targets at once.
* One of the best combo starters if used correctly, and can be easily followed by [[Flash Step]] to follow up with other moves.
* Quick start-up.
* [[Instinct/Break|Breaks Instinct]].
* Upgraded water shield is very effective in avoiding being damaged by jumpers.
* When held, the user gains a 70% damage reduction.
* Grants additional 35% damage reduction after the move.
* This move cannot be canceled by incoming damage, and will turn a portion of the damage received during the hold into temporary health. This converts into normal health after a while. (Does not need to be upgraded, but will be stronger when it is)
* Can be used to interrupt enemy combos and start combos (By holding).
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* It is hard to hit a moving opponent from far away, so it may require some prediction and skill.
* Bad M1s compared to other [[fighting Styles|fighting styles]].
** M1s have terrible hitboxes, long cooldowns, and dash at the third hit.
** Sometimes the third M1 won't even hit at all, unless the user is using [[Buddha]].
** The fourth M1 does not hit if Buddha Transformation is active.
* Severe lack of mobility.
* May be expensive in the [[Second Sea]].
* Relatively weak damage.

|'''[Z] Twelve Water Palms'''
* Short range.
* May bug with high ping or overexaggerated movement.
* Low mobility.
* Punishable endlag unless upgraded.
* No longer carries momentum. 
* Has a huge delay.

|'''[X] Pressure Vortex'''
* The bubble is single target.
* Slow travel speed.
* Sometimes, the shark may circle around the opponent without trapping them in a bubble.

|'''[C] Great Sea Spear'''
* Grants no I-frames.
* Small range.
* High knockback, making it unreliable for grinding.
* The upgrade requires the [[Headband (Black)]], which is relatively hard to obtain with it requiring 100% accuracy in the [[Fish Fights|Fish Fight]] against the [[Sharkman Master]].
* Temporary Health does not last very long.
}}
</tabber>

