==Trivia==
* Both [[Kilo Admiral]] and [[Fish Crew Member]] uses Sharkman Karate Old's M1's as its melee.
* Sharkman Karate is considerably one of the best ways to grind for [[Aura]] levels, as almost all the moves are tick damage, especially {{Ability|C}} as it has lots of tick damage.
* Sharkman Karate is the second V2 [[Fighting Styles|Fighting Style]] to have an upgraded version, the first being [[Dragon Talon]].
* Before [[Updates/27.2|Update 27.2]], Sharkman Karate was obtained from Daigrock, the Sharkman.
* Despite being an upgrade to [[Water Kung Fu]], Sharkman Karate's M1’s are not considered worth using by the community due to its dash. It is recommended to use Sharkman Karate solely for PvP, and [[Water Kung Fu]] for grinding since it’s spammable.
* Currently, the Sharkman Master's final belt in the [[Fish Fights|Fish Fight]] battle training is excruciatingly hard to obtain, as it requires a 100% critical hit ratio, and involves luck over the Sharkman Master misses his final hit.
* Sharkman Karate shared very similar visual effects with awakened [[Flame]]'s '''[Z] Burning Blast''', (prior to it's revamp) as it shared the same meshes and almost seemed like a recolored version.
* This also applies for old Sharkman Karate's [C] Move having similar effects to awakened [[Flame]]'s {{Ability|Flame|X|1}}, most likely due to it being a very old fighting style.
